If I ask someone what surrounds the building, they'll answer "a bunch
of students" or "a group of students". "Bunch" will be used in the
sense of "group", and not in the sense that we've defined it for the
purposes of this conversation. I will less frequently get the answer
"fifty students", because it's seldom that people miss the forest for
the trees, or in this case the crowd for each student, and when I do
receive that answer, it'll be in the sense of "fifty students
together".

